 "overview": "The CC Historical Commission archive encompasses the proceedings of Medford's historical and historic district commissions, which oversee the protection, documentation, and regulation of the city's historic assets. Meeting records in the archive span from July 2023 to October 2026. Over this time, the bodies have evaluated residential and commercial properties under the demolition delay ordinance, pursued the establishment of local historic districts, and guided Community Preservation Act projects. Their work has also directed extensive archaeological investigations and gravestone conservation at historic burying grounds and Brooks family sites. At recent meetings, the commissions addressed a backlog of demolition applications, finalized recommendations on municipal zoning initiatives, and conducted commissioner recruitment and educational programming.",
