  {
   "name": "Demolition delay and historic significance reviews",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission regularly reviews demolition applications to determine historic significance and decide whether properties should be designated as preferably preserved, invoking an 18-month demolition delay [M07#2, M09#1]. Properties subject to delay proceedings have included 56 Wareham Street, 27 Allmont Street, 38 Pearl Street, and 110 Brooks Street [M09#1, M14#1, M15#4, M20#1]. In several cases, applicants worked with subcommittees on architectural modifications and design mitigation, leading the commission to approve lifting delays for structures such as 38 Pearl Street, 110 Brooks Street, 56 Wareham Street, and 47 Holton Street [M18#1, M22#1, M23#1, M28#9]. For other properties, including 15 Maple Park Avenue and 71 Mystic Avenue, the commission determined structures were not preferably preserved after public hearings, allowing demolition to proceed [M41#1, M41#2].",
