  {
   "name": "Cross Street Cemetery restoration and archaeology",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission pursued Community Preservation Act funding, historical research, and headstone restoration for Cross Street Cemetery [M03#5, M04#1, M08#5]. Exploratory trenching conducted at the former cemetery parcel uncovered artifacts and human remains, prompting multi-year state coordination, state archaeological permitting, and contracting with PAL [M20#6, M25#6]. The commission allocated funds for headstone assessments and veteran marker restoration, estimating substantial repair costs for relocated gravestones at Oak Grove Cemetery [M12#3, M25#5, M26#7]. Work later advanced to gravestone cleaning, front gate recreation plans, fence repairs, and preparations for ground-penetrating radar testing [M28#8, M33#3, M35#6, M39#5, M40#12].",
