  {
   "name": "Thomas Brooks Park archaeological preservation",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission initiated preservation plans for the archaeological site at Thomas Brooks Park, collaborating with consultant Peter Hedlund on design concepts including an archaeological cap, foundation tracing, and an accessible history walk [M08#3, M09#4, M10#3, M12#1]. Funding was secured through the Community Preservation Committee for Phase Two construction, including tree trimming, ADA sidewalk connections, and interpretive signage [M14#8, M21#3]. Consultant SWCA was selected for Phase Two archaeological work while public meetings gathered community input on park design and natural features [M21#4, M25#8]. Preservation efforts continued into 2026 with completed tree work and plans for ground-penetrating radar [M33#3, M35#6].",
