  {
   "name": "Preservation ordinances and citywide zoning coordination",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission examined preservation zoning models from other municipalities, such as Reading, to explore zoning relief incentives for property owners who preserve historic structures [M22#3, M23#5]. Commissioners monitored proposed municipal up-zoning, including the Salem Street corridor, and formed subcommittees to comment on proposed city zoning changes [M26#9, M27#5]. The bodies drafted opposition to state legislation, Senate Bill S993, citing concerns regarding restrictions on local oversight over historic demolitions [M29#4, M31#2]. Commission members later reviewed adopted Medford Square zoning incentives and finalized recommendations for the Boston Avenue zoning corridor [M33#1, M35#2, M40#10].",
